  "notes": "Cash basis village. Governmental lines from the Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances - Governmental Funds (p4, Total column); business-type lines from the proprietary funds statement (p6, Total column; Water, Sewer, Sanitation). Interest income and loan payments printed under Other Financing Sources (Uses) / Other Receipts (Disbursements) are recorded as receipts/disbursements outside the printed totals; loan proceeds 34,500 (Street) as debt_proceeds. Several 1-dollar rounding differences in the report itself (report_discrepancies). The only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budgetary comparison (p8), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental and proprietary fund statements. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement of assets and fund balances (p3; totals equal the government-wide figures), business-type lines from the proprietary funds statement (p5), totals from the Statement of Net Position (p1). Statement of cash flows (p7) is cash basis, so proprietary is null. Governmental identity: 73,192 + 293,453 - 275,026 + 34,500 = 126,119 vs 126,118 printed (report rounding). Business identity: 71,540 + 275,692 - 206,923 = 140,309. Read pages 1-8 of 8"
